{"body":{"text":["A component is a function of what it is given and of the field, and keeps no state of the field: \"The UI was always supposed to be stateless\" (21/63). What the browser keeps for convenience stands apart, how a list was last shown and whether the bar is open; whether it belongs in the field is the path State in buffers. A component is given `io`, the chassis's actions where it is drawn, passed in, since a free function would need hidden state to reach the chassis (21/43, 21/44), and taken by the author as something that just holds actions (21/49), though he likes no objects with methods (21/39); it is named after his word for what meets the outside, \"It's I/O\" (16/5): `read`, the field as it renders, the value, or nothing until it answers; `ask`, the field once, as a handler does; `draw`, a value within it, by whatever draws that; `propose`, a value back through the way back, committed; `remove`, it taken out of the list it stands in; and `pick`, where a component is to be chosen. \"We do need the consuming of the field in components to be simple\" (21/3); \"If I invoke a read, of course the chassis will be aware of me invoking a read. … And when it comes in, it's just a value. Why can't I use that value directly?\" (21/57). No helper stands between: \"I don't understand the point of live at all, of using a helper at all\" (21/55). *A component a plain function over values and stateless, the author's, 21/57 and 21/63; no helper his, 21/55; the actions the session's, he having asked for few (21/53, 21/54); `io` the session's offer, taken by the author (21/50, 21/51); built.*"]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The chassis does for every component what each would else do for itself, the reads being, in the author's words, the \"state management\" of the \"framework\" (21/31). The expressions every component reads in one turn it asks as one read of the engine, kept live, each told its own part of the answer, and each asked alone again where that one read fails; a read asked whole, as Answer's, is asked alone. It renders a component again when what it is given changes, or an answer says something new, and lays the new render over the page, changing only what differs, so focus, a caret and a scroll stay (21/60); keeps each drawing in place by its key, a holon by its id, a drawing by the uses it was reached through, the field giving the keys the author held lists need (21/29); shows a drawing made anew, or a render waiting on its reads, once every read within it has answered, so nothing shows piece by piece, or after two seconds; and stands each drawing as a boundary, the component Problem drawn in its place, given what failed, where what it is given, a read it asks or its render fails: \"failure handling as error boundaries make sense and that the chassis then mount the error component\" (21/39). Where the way back finds no change, the chassis marks the place fixed, `data-fixed` on its host, which no render of that drawing undoes. It draws nothing of its own but a host for each drawing and a line where even Problem cannot draw; the inspector and the bar showing the page busy are the page's (21/32, 21/36). A component for waiting, a skeleton, waits: \"a waiting component has to be unique for that component and that enters the whole dilemma of good DX\" (21/41), the path Skeletons while waiting; so do reads streamed as they come, which the author finds an interesting possibility \"as long as it shows it is still rendering\" (21/29). A component holding what the browser keeps for it, as the input does with what is typed and what completion offers, gives its node with how to update it, and is updated in place of rendering. *Problems as boundaries with a component of their own, the author's (21/39); batching as the framework's state his (21/31); keys for lists his (21/29); a render only where something changed on his ground, \"The UI should only update if it's actually a change that actually changes\" (21/57); waiting before showing the session's, the author placing it with batching in the chassis (21/28, 21/31); the morph and the mark fixed the session's (21/60, 21/74), the last at his \"Don't ship broken things\" (21/73); built, 271 tests passing.*"]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component's look is its surface's, and shipped with the components, not with the site: \"the components look probably should be shipped with them. That's the component's responsibility\" (19/15). Styling has its degree, the author said, while what looks wholly different may want other components; so the look's variables are opened, to be tuned, by a knob component perhaps, and later taken from the field (19/15). On the web it stands in `components/web/look/`, a stylesheet for each component with a look of its own, beneath them the page's ground, all drawn with the chassis's tokens; one built stylesheet and the faces are what a site links, and beside it the chassis's own, in `chassis/web/look/`, and the inspector's, the page's, in `site/`; the bar showing the page busy keeps its look among the components'. The material, a stylesheet kept as text in glass that nothing read, was let go with its type: \"I don't see the point of the material\" (19/13, 19/15). *The look shipped with the components, its variables opened and the material let go, the author's, 19/15; its layout the session's; built.*"]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y002","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The chassis's look holds its tokens, which every component draws with and a site tunes, and what the chassis makes itself, a drawing's host and a line where even Problem could not draw, in `chassis/web/look/`. A link is made in one place, `chassis/web/href.ts`, as the page keeps its address, and no component reads the address: an answer says what was asked by its steps, as the pills say them, and a list keeps how it was shown by what it holds. The breadcrumb is one read of `wholes`, its names in one round after, and the start one of `roots`, functions written in the language. *The session's, at the author's word to clean what it could before he reviews (20/21); built.*"]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y003","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Layout as data was held to the test of the search bar, which takes a query and shows its steps as pills: `steps` gives the query's steps, `each` makes one use of the pill per step, and a list lays them beside an input; removing a pill flows back through the way back of each, then `chain`, then `print`, into the address (18/72). The pill and the input are code at the leaves, the arrangement around them data. \"if it can't, then we have a problem with layout as data\" (18/71). Built, the test came out mixed: the arrangement is data, the reader laying search above the answer and search laying the text's steps as pills beside the input, both shipped in glass, while the leaves, pill, input, list and answer, the ways back through each, steps and chain, and dropping an item from a list when its × is pressed are code (18/98). *Proposed, 18/72; built.* Pills taken from the text itself, given plain text, were weighed and not taken, print's tidying kept at the author's doubt (21/66, 21/67): the path Pills from the text."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y004","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Since components render on the chassis, a move takes about 95 to 220 ms in the browser, where it took 45 to 150: the path Moves slower than before. Timed step by step (21/84): the query committed, the root read again while the reads of the page before ran again, a component found by type in 20 to 33 ms (the path Finding by type on every move), then reads waiting on the reads before them, the 79 functions about 50 ms of it and a list's table a second round after its cards (the path The table's second round). Every kept read is worked out again, whole, whenever a store it stood on moves, and every read stands on every store; component renders are already only where something changed, the waste the engine's, as the session found (21/89). The author's view: only reads receiving a change should run again, \"not the whole page\" (21/77), \"only the changes should be broadcasted\" (21/83). A store telling, with its head, what its commits touched, and a kept read running again only where it read one, was built and reverted for losing changes silently (21/93), under the author's rule: \"It is important the engine does not get convoluted and no debt is made. Solutions must be pristine and simple and thought through under the principles and values of the system\" (21/86). *That rule settled, 21/86.* A kept read checking again, by content, the holons it used was weighed and held by the session, its gain too small for a second path in the engine (21/95), against his condition, \"if it is simple and provides strong benefit it makes sense\" (21/94): the path A kept read checking what it used. Re-deriving only where a change flows is, the author says, \"for the future … probably a requirement of an engine\" (21/90), the bigger step its successor (21/96). *Leaning, 21/90; open, the thread Reads re-derived where a change flows.* The engine keeps no state so that stores may become effective enough to stand apart: \"the stores themselves could be effective enough to be external, but that is a very long time\" (21/75)."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y005","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The query is a buffer, holding only the present, kept as one with the address, `?q=`: loading, back and forward type the address into it, each change replaces the address, and pressing Enter, taking out a pill or following a link pushes a step, so a link moves within the page and the engine keeps running. What is typed goes back, on Enter, from where the input is drawn to the buffer's text, which alone is written; as one types, only completion is offered. The page names its stores in its own code, as the author leaned: \"the site that we want built will define its stores in the sites. ts i would think\" (11/7), and took at 18/17: \"on point three: ok\". *Settled, 18/17.*"]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y006","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**page:** what hosts glass in a browser, and decides little."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y007","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**reader:** the component the page draws, search above the answer, given the query's text."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y008","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**pill:** one step of a query, shown in the bar."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y009","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**breadcrumb:** where the page stands, from home through the wholes above the holon the reader shows, each a way up; at rest, the top of the page."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y00A","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**λ:** the expression button at the breadcrumb's end, opening the bar in its place."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y00B","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**inspector:** what right-click opens, the page's: the place clicked, the component drawing it, the uses it was reached through, and the holon it shows."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y00C","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**look:** how components look on one surface, shipped with them, drawn with the chassis's tokens, opened as variables."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y00D","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**problem:** the component the chassis draws in place of a drawing that failed, given what failed."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y00E","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**morph:** a component's new render laid over the one shown, changing only what differs, so what the browser keeps stays."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y00F","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**home:** the start of the page, the field's roots, where every breadcrumb begins; the page also still mounts a store of that name in the browser."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y00G","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**site:** a page that starts glass upon stores it names."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y00H","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**brief:** a holon of knowledge giving one understanding, the smaller ones beneath it."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y00J","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**face:** a brief placed in another's flow, the start of a reading of its own."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y00K","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**thread:** a question held open in the field, with where it stands."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y00M","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**session:** a stretch of work with the author, kept whole in his words."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y00N","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**cycle:** a stretch of a session with one purpose, marked and condensed."]},"id":"1M86JG95095Y00P","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
